      "problem": "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to \\pi }\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=\\pi $ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\pi }\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
